- `signal.NotifyContext` cancels `ctx` on Ctrl+C (SIGINT) and on SIGTERM, which is what `docker stop` and systemd send.
- `srv.Shutdown` stops accepting new connections and waits for running requests to finish, at most 10 seconds here.
- `http.ErrServerClosed` is the normal return value of `ListenAndServe` after `Shutdown`, so it isn't treated as an error.
- An explicit `http.Server` also lets you set `ReadHeaderTimeout`, which protects against clients that send headers extremely slowly.

Use `net/http/httptest`: a `ResponseRecorder` captures what the handler writes, and you call `ServeHTTP` directly. Route the requests through the mux, though, because `r.PathValue("id")` is only filled in when the mux matched the pattern.

To make that easy, move the three `HandleFunc` lines from `main` into a method on `store` and use `Handler: s.routes()` in `main`:

```go
func (s *store) routes() *http.ServeMux {
	mux := http.NewServeMux()
	mux.HandleFunc("GET /todos", s.list)
	mux.HandleFunc("GET /todos/{id}", s.get)
	mux.HandleFunc("POST /todos", s.create)
	return mux
}
```

